---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import '../styles/globals.css'

const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
    "name": "Laso",
    "alternateName": "Laso Health",
    "applicationCategory": "HealthApplication",
    "operatingSystem": "iOS",
    "offers": {
      "@type": "Offer",
      "price": "0",
      "priceCurrency": "USD",
      "description": "Free 7-day trial, then $29.99/year"
    },
    "description": "Health intelligence app that turns Apple Watch, Oura, Garmin, and WHOOP data into daily recovery scores, strain targets, sleep debt tracking, stress monitoring, illness prediction, and biological age. All processed on-device.",
    "featureList": [
      "Recovery score based on HRV, resting heart rate, and sleep quality",
      "Strain tracking with recovery-adjusted daily targets",
      "Personalized sleep need and sleep debt tracking",
      "HRV-derived stress monitoring with guided breathwork",
      "Illness prediction 2-3 days before symptoms",
      "Biological age (Vitality Age) computed from 9 key health metrics",
      "86 health metrics across 8 categories",
      "What-if workout simulation",
      "Overtraining and burnout detection",
      "Menstrual cycle tracking with phase-specific training guidance",
      "On-device machine learning with personal baselines",
      "AES-256 encrypted, no cloud processing"
    ],
    "url": "https://lasohealth.fit",
    "image": "https://lasohealth.fit/og-image.png"
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "Laso Health",
    "url": "https://lasohealth.fit",
    "logo": "https://lasohealth.fit/favicon.svg",
    "sameAs": [
      "https://twitter.com/lasohealth"
    ],
    "contactPoint": {
      "@type": "ContactPoint",
      "email": "support@lasohealth.fit",
      "contactType": "customer support"
    }
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What is a recovery score and how does Laso calculate it?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "A recovery score (0–100) measures how ready your body is to perform. Laso calculates it from HRV (heart rate variability), resting heart rate, sleep quality, sleep duration, respiratory rate, and recent strain load. Unlike generic averages, Laso builds personal baselines calibrated to your body using on-device machine learning, so your score reflects your unique physiology."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How does strain tracking work in Laso?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Laso calculates a strain score from 0 to 21 based on heart rate zone distribution throughout the day. It then sets a personalized daily strain target based on your current recovery level. If recovery is high, Laso recommends a higher strain range so you can push harder. If recovery is low, the target drops so you can recover. The app also includes what-if simulation: you can preview how a planned workout would affect your recovery the next day."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What devices work with Laso?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Laso works with over 50 devices that sync to Apple Health, including Apple Watch, Oura Ring, Garmin, WHOOP, Fitbit, Polar, Samsung Galaxy Watch, COROS, Suunto, Withings, Ultrahuman Ring Air, Dexcom, Eight Sleep, and more. If your device writes data to Apple Health, Laso can read and analyze it. iPhone built-in sensors for steps and activity tracking also work without any wearable."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How does illness prediction work?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Laso monitors multiple health metrics simultaneously: HRV, resting heart rate, sleep patterns, respiratory rate, body temperature, and activity levels. When several of these metrics deviate from your personal baselines in a pattern consistent with immune system activation, Laso flags a potential illness signal 2 to 3 days before symptoms appear. The app also tracks 6 predictive health signals: fatigue, burnout, overtraining, insomnia risk, immune dip, and inactivity patterns."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What is Vitality Age and how is it different from biological age?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Vitality Age is Laso's biological age metric, computed daily from 9 key health indicators: VO2 Max, HRV, resting heart rate, sleep efficiency, deep sleep percentage, walking speed, daily steps, exercise minutes, and body composition. Unlike lab-based biological age tests that require blood draws, Vitality Age updates every day using data from your wearable. It shows whether you're aging faster or slower than your chronological age, tracks your 90-day trajectory, and identifies which 2–3 metrics to focus on to improve."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Is my health data private with Laso?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Yes. Every analysis in Laso runs entirely on your iPhone. No health data is sent to the cloud. All stored data is AES-256 encrypted with keys stored in the Secure Enclave. You don't even need to create an account to use the app. Laso reads data from Apple Health and processes it locally using on-device machine learning. No one sees your health data but you."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How is Laso different from WHOOP or Oura?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Three key differences: (1) No new hardware: Laso works with the wearable you already own (Apple Watch, Oura, Garmin, etc.), while WHOOP requires their $30/month band. (2) Broader analysis: Laso cross-analyzes 86 health metrics using causal inference (Granger causality), not just correlations. It covers recovery, strain, sleep, stress, illness prediction, biological age, and more in one app. (3) Complete privacy: all analysis runs on-device with no cloud processing, unlike WHOOP and Oura which require cloud accounts."
        }
      }
    ]
  }
]
---

<Base
  title="Laso.Recovery Score, Strain Tracking, Sleep Coaching & Health Intelligence for Apple Watch, Oura, Garmin"
  description="Laso turns Apple Watch, Oura, Garmin, and WHOOP data into daily recovery scores, strain targets, sleep debt tracking, illness prediction, and biological age. 86 health metrics analyzed on-device. Private. No new hardware needed."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="min-h-screen bg-white">
    <header>
    <!-- ════════ NAV ════════ -->
    <nav aria-label="Main navigation" class="nav-blur fixed top-0 inset-x-0 z-50 border-b border-gray-100/60">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-5 h-12 flex items-center justify-between">
        <a href="#" class="text-[22px] font-bold tracking-tight text-apple-dark hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity">Laso</a>
        <div class="hidden sm:flex items-center gap-7">
          <a href="#features" class="text-[13px] font-medium text-apple-secondary hover:text-apple-dark transition-colors">Features</a>
          <a href="#devices" class="text-[13px] font-medium text-apple-secondary hover:text-apple-dark transition-colors">Devices</a>
        </div>
        <a href="#early-access" class="bg-apple-dark text-white text-xs font-medium rounded-full px-4 py-1.5 hover:bg-black transition-colors">
          Get Early Access
        </a>
      </div>
    </nav>
    </header>

    <main>
    <!-- ════════ HERO ════════ -->
    <section data-section="hero" class="hero-gradient pt-32 pb-16 md:pt-44 md:pb-24 px-5 text-center">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-apple-blue/10 text-apple-blue text-sm font-medium rounded-full px-4 py-1.5 mb-6">
        <span class="w-2 h-2 bg-apple-blue rounded-full animate-pulse"></span>
        iOS Early Access Open
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl lg:text-7xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-apple-dark text-balance max-w-4xl mx-auto leading-[1.08]">
        Health scores that are
        <span class="gradient-text">actually about you.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lg md:text-xl text-apple-secondary max-w-2xl mx-auto text-balance leading-relaxed">
        Laso learns what's normal for your body and tells you what to do about it. Recovery, strain, sleep, stress, illness risk. All from the wearable you already own.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 max-w-md mx-auto">
        <form id="hero-form" class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3">
          <input
            type="email"
            placeholder="your@email.com"
            required
            class="hero-email-input flex-1 rounded-full border border-gray-200 px-5 py-3 text-[15px] text-apple-dark placeholder:text-apple-secondary/50 focus:outline-none focus:border-apple-blue focus:ring-1 focus:ring-apple-blue/30 transition-colors"
          />
          <button
            type="submit"
            class="bg-apple-dark text-white font-medium rounded-full px-7 py-3 text-[15px] hover:bg-black transition-colors active:scale-[0.97] cursor-pointer shrink-0"
          >
            Join Early Access
          </button>
        </form>
        <p class="hero-success mt-3 text-sm text-emerald-600 font-medium hidden">You're in! We'll be in touch soon.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[13px] text-apple-secondary/60">Free 7-day trial. <strong class="text-apple-dark"><span class="signup-counter">550</span> have joined</strong>.</p>
      </div>
      <!-- Hero trust strip -->
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-5 text-[13px] text-apple-secondary/70">
        <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" class="w-4 h-4"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75 11.25 15 15 9.75m-3-7.036A11.959 11.959 0 0 1 3.598 6 11.99 11.99 0 0 0 3 9.749c0 5.592 3.824 10.29 9 11.623 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.31-.21-2.571-.598-3.751h-.152c-3.196 0-6.1-1.248-8.25-3.285Z"/></svg>
          100% on-device
        </span>
        <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" class="w-4 h-4"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M10.5 1.5H8.25A2.25 2.25 0 0 0 6 3.75v16.5a2.25 2.25 0 0 0 2.25 2.25h7.5A2.25 2.25 0 0 0 18 20.25V3.75a2.25 2.25 0 0 0-2.25-2.25H13.5m-3 0V3h3V1.5m-3 0h3"/></svg>
          50+ devices supported
        </span>
        <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" class="w-4 h-4"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M18.364 18.364A9 9 0 0 0 5.636 5.636m12.728 12.728A9 9 0 0 1 5.636 5.636m12.728 12.728L5.636 5.636"/></svg>
          No account required
        </span>
      </div>

    </section>

    <!-- ════════ YOUR MORNING BRIEF ════════ -->
    <section data-section="brief" class="bg-apple-gray py-20 md:py-28 px-5">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="section-reveal text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-apple-dark text-center text-balance">
          Every morning, five numbers that actually mean something.
        </h2>
        <p class="section-reveal mt-4 text-center text-apple-secondary text-[15px] md:text-base max-w-xl mx-auto">
          Each one is compared to your own history. Not an age group average, not a generic benchmark. Your data, your baseline.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-14 grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-5 gap-4">
          <div class="section-reveal bg-white rounded-2xl p-5 text-center">
            <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-2xl bg-emerald-50 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5" class="w-6 h-6"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75 11.25 15 15 9.75M21 12a9 9 0 1 1-18 0 9 9 0 0 1 18 0Z"/></svg>
            </div>
            <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-emerald-600">84</p>
            <p class="text-xs font-medium text-apple-dark mt-1">Recovery</p>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-apple-secondary mt-0.5">Above your baseline</p>
          </div>

          <div class="section-reveal bg-white rounded-2xl p-5 text-center" style="transition-delay:60ms">
            <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-2xl bg-indigo-50 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#6366f1" stroke-width="1.5" class="w-6 h-6"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M21.752 15.002A9.72 9.72 0 0 1 18 15.75c-5.385 0-9.75-4.365-9.75-9.75 0-1.33.266-2.597.748-3.752A9.753 9.753 0 0 0 3 11.25C3 16.635 7.365 21 12.75 21a9.753 9.753 0 0 0 9.002-5.998Z"/></svg>
            </div>
            <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-indigo-600">7h 42m</p>
            <p class="text-xs font-medium text-apple-dark mt-1">Sleep</p>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-apple-secondary mt-0.5">96% of your need</p>
          </div>

          <div class="section-reveal bg-white rounded-2xl p-5 text-center" style="transition-delay:120ms">
            <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-2xl bg-orange-50 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#f97316" stroke-width="1.5" class="w-6 h-6"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15.362 5.214A8.252 8.252 0 0 1 12 21 8.25 8.25 0 0 1 6.038 7.047 8.287 8.287 0 0 0 9 9.601a8.983 8.983 0 0 1 3.361-6.867 8.21 8.21 0 0 0 3 2.48Z"/></svg>
            </div>
            <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-orange-500">8.4</p>
            <p class="text-xs font-medium text-apple-dark mt-1">Strain</p>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-apple-secondary mt-0.5">Target: 8–12</p>
          </div>

          <div class="section-reveal bg-white rounded-2xl p-5 text-center" style="transition-delay:180ms">
            <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-2xl bg-yellow-50 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#eab308" stroke-width="1.5" class="w-6 h-6"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9.813 15.904 9 18.75l-.813-2.846a4.5 4.5 0 0 0-3.09-3.09L2.25 12l2.846-.813a4.5 4.5 0 0 0 3.09-3.09L9 5.25l.813 2.846a4.5 4.5 0 0 0 3.09 3.09L15.75 12l-2.846.813a4.5 4.5 0 0 0-3.09 3.09Z"/></svg>
            </div>
            <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-yellow-600">Low</p>
            <p class="text-xs font-medium text-apple-dark mt-1">Stress</p>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-apple-secondary mt-0.5">Below your normal</p>
          </div>

          <div class="section-reveal bg-white rounded-2xl p-5 text-center col-span-2 md:col-span-1" style="transition-delay:240ms">
            <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-2xl bg-green-50 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="1.5" class="w-6 h-6"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m4.5 12.75 6 6 9-13.5"/></svg>
            </div>
            <p class="text-2xl font-bold text-green-600">Clear</p>
            <p class="text-xs font-medium text-apple-dark mt-1">Health Risks</p>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-apple-secondary mt-0.5">No warnings</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="section-reveal mt-6 text-xs text-apple-secondary/50 text-center">Sample daily brief. All values based on your personal data.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ════════ YOU ARE THE BASELINE ════════ -->
    <section data-section="baseline" class="py-20 md:py-28 px-5">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="section-reveal text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-apple-dark text-center text-balance">
          Why most health apps get it wrong.
        </h2>
        <p class="section-reveal mt-4 text-center text-apple-secondary text-[15px] md:text-base max-w-xl mx-auto">
          They compare you to a population average. So someone with a naturally low HRV gets told they're "below average" every single day, even when they're feeling great. Laso compares you to you.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-14 grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          <!-- Other Apps -->
          <div class="section-reveal rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6 md:p-7 relative overflow-hidden">
            <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 right-0 h-1 bg-gray-300"></div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-apple-secondary uppercase tracking-wider mb-5">Typical health app</p>
            <div class="space-y-4">
              <div>
                <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-1.5">
                  <span class="text-sm font-medium text-apple-dark">Your HRV</span>
                  <span class="text-lg font-bold text-apple-dark">42 ms</span>
                </div>
                <div class="w-full h-2 bg-gray-100 rounded-full overflow-hidden">
                  <div class="h-full bg-red-400 rounded-full" style="width: 62%"></div>
                </div>
                <div class="flex items-center justify-between mt-1.5">
                  <span class="text-[11px] text-apple-secondary">Population avg: <strong>55 ms</strong></span>
                  <span class="text-[11px] font-semibold text-red-500">Below Average</span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="border-t border-gray-100 pt-4">
                <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#d1d5db" stroke-width="1.5" class="w-4 h-4 mt-0.5 shrink-0"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 9v3.75m9-.75a9 9 0 1 1-18 0 9 9 0 0 1 18 0Zm-9 3.75h.008v.008H12v-.008Z"/></svg>
                  <p class="text-sm text-apple-secondary">"Try meditation and reduce stress."</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Laso -->
          <div class="section-reveal rounded-2xl border border-emerald-200 bg-white p-6 md:p-7 relative overflow-hidden" style="transition-delay:120ms">
            <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 right-0 h-1 bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-400 to-cyan-400"></div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-apple-blue uppercase tracking-wider mb-5">Laso</p>
            <div class="space-y-4">
              <div>
                <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-1.5">
                  <span class="text-sm font-medium text-apple-dark">Your HRV</span>
                  <span class="text-lg font-bold text-apple-dark">42 ms</span>
                </div>
                <div class="w-full h-2 bg-gray-100 rounded-full overflow-hidden">
                  <div class="h-full bg-emerald-500 rounded-full" style="width: 88%"></div>
                </div>
                <div class="flex items-center justify-between mt-1.5">
                  <span class="text-[11px] text-apple-secondary">Your baseline: <strong>38 ms</strong></span>
                  <span class="text-[11px] font-semibold text-emerald-600">+10% Above Your Normal</span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="border-t border-emerald-100 pt-4">
                <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5" class="w-4 h-4 mt-0.5 shrink-0"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75 11.25 15 15 9.75M21 12a9 9 0 1 1-18 0 9 9 0 0 1 18 0Z"/></svg>
                  <p class="text-sm text-apple-dark font-medium">"Recovery is high. Good day to push it. Aim for strain 12-16."</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="section-reveal mt-8 text-center text-sm text-apple-secondary max-w-lg mx-auto">
          Same person. Same number. One app says you're behind. The other knows this is actually a good week for you.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ════════ DAILY ACTIONS ════════ -->
    <section data-section="actions" class="bg-apple-gray py-20 md:py-28 px-5">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="section-reveal text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-apple-dark text-center text-balance">
          It tells you what to do, not just what happened.
        </h2>
        <p class="section-reveal mt-4 text-center text-apple-secondary text-[15px] md:text-base max-w-xl mx-auto">
          Here's what a morning with Laso actually looks like.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-12 max-w-2xl mx-auto space-y-4">
          <div class="section-reveal flex items-start gap-4 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 p-5">
            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5" class="w-5 h-5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15.362 5.214A8.252 8.252 0 0 1 12 21 8.25 8.25 0 0 1 6.038 7.047 8.287 8.287 0 0 0 9 9.601a8.983 8.983 0 0 1 3.361-6.867 8.21 8.21 0 0 0 3 2.48Z"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="text-[15px] font-semibold text-apple-dark">"Recovery 84. Good day to go hard."</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-apple-secondary mt-1">Your HRV is up 14% from where it usually sits. Laso sets your strain target to 12-16. Go run, lift, whatever you want.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="section-reveal flex items-start gap-4 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 p-5" style="transition-delay:80ms">
            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-indigo-50 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#6366f1" stroke-width="1.5" class="w-5 h-5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M21.752 15.002A9.72 9.72 0 0 1 18 15.75c-5.385 0-9.75-4.365-9.75-9.75 0-1.33.266-2.597.748-3.752A9.753 9.753 0 0 0 3 11.25C3 16.635 7.365 21 12.75 21a9.753 9.753 0 0 0 9.002-5.998Z"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="text-[15px] font-semibold text-apple-dark">"You're 45 min short on sleep. Bed by 10:30 tonight."</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-apple-secondary mt-1">Laso figured out you need 7h 50m, not the usual "8 hours everyone says." Go to bed 20 min earlier for 3 nights and you're caught up.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="section-reveal flex items-start gap-4 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 p-5" style="transition-delay:160ms">
            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-amber-50 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.5" class="w-5 h-5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 9v3.75m-9.303 3.376c-.866 1.5.217 3.374 1.948 3.374h14.71c1.73 0 2.813-1.874 1.948-3.374L13.949 3.378c-.866-1.5-3.032-1.5-3.898 0L2.697 16.126ZM12 15.75h.007v.008H12v-.008Z"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="text-[15px] font-semibold text-apple-dark">"Your HRV has been dropping for 3 days. Take it easy."</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-apple-secondary mt-1">Down 15% from your normal. That usually means you're overdoing it. Keep strain under 8 today, walk or stretch, and check back tomorrow.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

